WEBVTT

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:48.630
Next, let's look at some
properties in this region.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.010
Is it just me, or is it kinda hot here?

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.930
Perhaps you should take that off, then.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.100
Oh.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.180
"Property #5:
A Community of Homes"

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:08.320
I definitely like warm places
like this way better!

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.730
I see, so you dislike cold climates.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.320
You're fine abandoning
the igloo you built, then?

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.410
Yeah.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:17.160
The yetis were glad
to take it off my claws.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.370
Is that so?

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.250
For our next potential property, then,

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:28.460
I believe you'd fare well
in a communal living arrangement,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.300
so I had planned on reaching out
to a few landlords I'm acquainted with...

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:37.220
But their communities are
oriented towards bachelors.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.140
Papa!

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.180
I'm a bachelor!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:39.890
Papa!

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.060
I'm not your Papa!

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.850
Here you are, Letty.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:44.560
Huh?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.310
To celebrate the birth of your first-born.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.440
Oh, thank you so much!

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.730
Wait!

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.860
What kind of home would you
like to share with your Papa?

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.490
What did I <i>just </i>say?!

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:57.570
As I've mentioned before, Letty,

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.580
sometimes, when a creature is born,
it imprints onto the first person it sees.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.160
R-Right.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.540
It's nigh-impossible to reverse
the effects of imprinting.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.330
Y-Yeah, but...

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.340
Do you really think it's okay
for me to raise it as my own?

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.340
Oh, Letty.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.430
I know a story on this very topic.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.050
Long, long ago,

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:22.390
there once was a human explorer who,
during an expedition into the woods,

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.770
came upon a gigantic egg.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.190
From that egg hatched a monstrous bird.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:35.110
The bird, believing the human was its
mother, began to follow him everywhere.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:40.490
The explorer tried to return it
to the wild countless times,

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.910
but the bird was determined
to stay with him.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:48.620
And so, the explorer raised the bird
as if it were his own child.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.210
The bird lived alongside him,
believing it, too, was human.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.210
Father!

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.920
Wow, imprinting is no joke!

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.510
However, the bird did not understand
that humans lived short lives,

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.300
Father!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:05.180
so when the explorer died,
it stayed with the corpse.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:10.850
Some say that, even now, you can
hear it calling "Father! Father!"

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.060
Father...

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:14.610
And an insistent pecking. Bang, bang...

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.530
What happened to the feel-good story?!

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:19.410
Even if half of that story is made-up...

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.870
Wait, which half is true?!

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.620
Once it has imprinted upon someone,
the chick cannot be returned to its parents.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.080
The first half? The last half?!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.960
You brought it with you because
you realized that, correct?

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:34.920
Luckily, that's a hraesvelgr chick.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.130
It will grow up just fine without
much intervention on your part.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.130
Hooray... what?

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.340
A giant eagle with an affinity for cold.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.060
They live along rivers
in the northern mountain region.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.520
Their chicks eat snow until they're
old enough to leave the nest.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.190
Wow!

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:54.020
Once it's full-grown, you needn't
worry about looking after it.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.740
It can summon a blizzard
with one flap of its wings.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.320
It will survive just fine on its own.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.360
Somehow, that makes me even <i>more </i>worried!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.830
All you need to be concerned with now
is keeping it cool and feeding it snow.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.080
Quite simple, yes?

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.080
Sure, but there isn't any
snow or ice around here.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.500
Again, simple, yes?

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.800
Yeah, simple.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.760
Still...

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.970
I'll probably still screw up somehow.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.400
In that case, my idea
may work in your favor.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.400
Huh?

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.440
Perhaps here...

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.780
...we can find a parent more
suited to raising this chick.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:58.340
Wow! I've never been to
a housing community before!

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.760
The price for a home
in a community like this

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.380
is much lower than an independent unit.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.890
Communal living means you can
rely on your neighbors for help.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:10.520
As such, this would be a wonderful
place for your little one.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:14.440
However, there aren't many units
that can house larger creatures.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:18.400
Most units are designed
for small to mid-size beings.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.240
Why are there so few for bigger people?

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.240
A dragon?!

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.400
Whoa, a dragon!

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.910
They can destroy common areas
with the slightest of movements,

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.240
Gotta send this... oops!

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.240
leading to increased repair costs.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.660
Oh.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:38.420
Larger creatures tend to be louder
as well, leading to noise complaints.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:38.420
Damn neighbors!

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:40.420
Sorry 'bout that...

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.970
Larger species don't typically live in
communal groups like smaller species do,

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.680
so there's less demand.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.470
Does that mean the Heroes
come to raid here, too?

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.350
Unfortunately, less, but not that often.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.560
All right, chumps! Time to clean house!

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.100
Ah, speak of the devil.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.690
What, not gonna put up a fight?!

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.430
A wild HERO appeared!

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.230
Hand over all yer rare items!

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:04.570
Are they gonna be okay, Dearia?!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.320
C'mon, fight me, ya cowa--

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.490
Hey!

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:12.750
The hell are you doin' to my tenants?!

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:13.950
I'm already dead!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.870
The landlords will take
care of them in most cases.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.710
Oh, wow.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:22.090
Most assailants are comprised of Heroes
tired of their typical adventuring,

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:26.550
who raid the community
as a form of New Game Plus raid.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.180
Don't they realize they're a nuisance?!

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.800
Come, friends! Today,
we pillage every dwelling!

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:31.680
Yeah!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:32.890
Here we go again.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.980
Agents of Darkness!
Your luck runs thin this day!

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:39.230
We will purge the earth of your filth by--

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:42.650
All the landlords here are quite powerful.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:44.690
Thank you, sir!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:49.240
Don't mention it. Let me know
if I can help with anything.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.660
The strong protect
the weak who can't fight...

00:07:54.660 --> 00:08:00.130
Don't worry, I'm gonna find
the best Mama and Papa for you!

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.630
Landlord the First

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.890
Oh, I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
our complex can't house...

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.770
...larger creat-- oh!

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:17.390
Dearia! It's been too long.

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:18.730
It's good to see you again.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:22.770
I'm so glad you're doing well.
And who is this with you?

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.150
Hello, I'm Letty.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.950
I have a different matter
to discuss with you today.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.860
Oh, really?

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:33.080
You're looking for adoptive parents?

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.250
I've never met a dragon
this caring before.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:38.960
C'mon, sweetie, I think it's lovely!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.460
Sure, I'll give you that.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.630
Right? Then we can totally take it in!

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.090
Are they, uh, married?

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.670
No, they're not married.

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:45.670
I don't know...

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.050
Aww, c'mon, why not?

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.050
Because they have differing tastes,

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:51.090
Look, hon, it's not that easy.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:51.090
it's hard for two-headed creatures
to find romantic partners.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.470
It could be!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:54.760
So these brothers pretend to be
a married couple to make up for that.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.760
I know, but...

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.810
That's so sad!

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:01.400
You know we'd do
anything for you, Dearia...

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:05.570
But lots of our residents
have been high-strung lately.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:11.780
We just had issues with a tenant
complaining someone's kids were loud.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:16.450
And my hearing's been going.
Dunno if I can take care of a kid.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:17.950
Oh, sweetie...

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:23.920
W-Well, it's only just hatched,
so I don't think it'll cry that loud.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:27.340
That's true! Look how
small and cute it is.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:31.510
I suppose it wouldn't be too much hassle
takin' care of something this little.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.180
Whaddya say, little guy?

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:41.270
Papa!

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.050
Chick used CRY!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.050
It's super effective!!

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:46.610
Bro! Are you okay?!

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:49.530
Hang in there, dude!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:52.020
Landlord the Second

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:54.410
Oh, my!

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:59.160
You're looking for a mom for your
little hatchling? You're so sweet!

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.040
It, uh... cries pretty loud, though.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.170
That just means he's a healthy boy!

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:11.670
Everyone in our building has kids, so I
doubt anyone would complain about him.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.720
How about I take
this little fellow in, then?

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:16.300
You mean it?!

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:19.850
Why don't you come in for a bit,
have some tea? We can chat there.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.730
Just a damn second!

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.520
You're bringing in <i>another </i>pet?!

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.770
You know the HOA doesn't allow pets!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:32.030
It's not a pet, it's my
beautiful son! How rude!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:36.450
The gall of you, I swear!

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:39.160
And I suppose you'll boast about
your cage discipline, then?

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:42.040
Is that how you treat your children?!

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:46.330
Our residents always complain
about our unit smelling like a zoo!

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.340
My, are you sure it's not
<i>you </i>they're smelling?

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.880
If anyone smells like a zoo,
it's you, you filthy cow!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.880
And you don't smell like rotting fish,
you disgusting snake?

00:10:55.880 --> 00:11:00.510
Perhaps you wouldn't be so stuck-up
if you weren't flat as a board!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.810
The hell did you just say
to me, you nasty hag?!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.810
This could get ugly!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.310
L-Let's take a deep breath, okay?

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.190
Shut it, you big lizard!

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.770
You wanna die?!

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.480
Mind your own damn business!

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.360
I'm sorry!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.030
They're scarier than the Heroes!

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:17.660
Seems this will take a while.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.280
Let's go speak to someone else.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.450
Okay.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.410
Landlord the Third

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:28.000
I see. I'd be happy
to take the little one in.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.550
I have many children of my own.
I'm sure they'll become fast friends!

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:37.300
Come now, children, say hello.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.680
Hello!

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.970
Hello! Would you like to play together?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.060
We'd love to!

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:48.730
It won't be lonely here, that's for sure.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.270
Indeed not.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:55.820
I'm so glad. We finally found
a good home for you!

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:04.200
Um, uh, is that okay?

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.040
Huh?!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.170
Papa!

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.170
Dinner time!

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.420
Oh, they're just play-biting.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:20.090
Just a bit of rough-housing, nothing more!

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.810
Yeah, right! Look behind you!
See how their eyes are glowing?!

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:30.480
Where should we go next?

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.020
...Lord!

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.940
Flame Dragon Lord!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.110
Huh?

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:43.030
Down here, Flame Dragon Lord!

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:45.660
Fancy seeing you here, milord!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.250
I know you!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:52.290
You're the korpukkur from back then!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.840
What are you doing here?

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:58.380
We come by every now and then
to sell the fruits of our labor.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.090
I never imagined we'd meet again here!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:04.850
What business has
brought you here, milord?

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:08.980
I-I'm looking for adoptive
parents for a baby.

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:12.810
Oh, then please, let us
help you with that endeavor!

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:17.940
Could you wait here for a moment?
We'll be back as soon as we deliver this.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:20.320
Th-Thanks!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.990
So, uh, what is that?

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:26.580
Oh, this? Well...

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:29.580
It's a wildfowl we hunted ourselves!

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:34.540
Subduing the fierce beast was tough,
but it's of a quite high quality!

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:38.420
So, what's the child
you're fostering like?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.510
Oh, uh...

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:48.810
A-Actually, I think I'll hold off on
finding someone to adopt it for now.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:50.020
Huh?!

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:51.850
Till we meet again!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.850
Flame Dragon Lord!

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:58.570
Thank you so very much
for offering to help.

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:00.070
O-Of course.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.610
Landlord the Fourth

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:06.660
So that's the story;
you need someone to adopt it?

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:10.700
Yeah, this little guy needs a home.
What do you think?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.210
He's a very good boy.

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:16.880
Boy, I bet this little guy
could get swole in no time.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:18.630
Get on up here.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:27.050
I'm gonna whip you into shape!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.890
Next up, grab this, kiddo!

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:36.650
O-Oh, no! If I don't
stop him, it's gonna...

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:39.480
It's gonna be ripped!

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:40.900
And I won't have that!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.280
What? You changed your mind?

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.200
Yeah.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:46.570
And here I thought you were
serious about training.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.700
I don't do demos, y'know.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.490
Sorry 'bout that.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:18.440
Aww, man...

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:21.070
It sure isn't going the way I'd hoped.

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.150
It would seem not.

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:34.790
I wonder how it got separated
from its parents in the first place.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:38.040
After hraesvelgr lay
their eggs in the snow,

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:43.460
they keep their nests hidden
by staying away until the eggs hatch.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:48.050
Most likely, this one was in a bad spot,
so it emerged from its buried nest.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.430
Aww.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:56.350
If I'd just left it alone, maybe its
mommy would've come back for it.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:16:01.730
It's certainly possible,
but very unlikely.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:07.200
Had you left the egg there,
some other creature would have eaten it.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:13.830
I believe the only reason it's still
alive is because you protected it.

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:16.790
I guess.

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.370
Why don't <i>you </i>raise it, Letty?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:23.500
B-B-Because I don't think it would
want me to be its Papa!

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.800
I'm a weak, cowardly dragon.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:32.510
I probably couldn't protect it
if something happened to us.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:35.560
I'd be a bad dad.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.850
You're right. It may not want you.

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.100
You're not supposed to agree with me!

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.400
I knew it...

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:45.530
However, I think all
parents feel that way.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.030
Huh?

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:50.030
No one is perfect from the start.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.530
One only learns and grows as a parent

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:57.250
by laughing, crying, and
worrying alongside their child.

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:02.540
And strength and bravery are not
the only things that make a good father.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:06.300
Though in terms of protection,
nothing trumps physical strength.

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:07.760
Yeah, thought so.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.630
Oh, there you are!

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:18.230
I heard you'd come for a visit, Dearia!

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:20.440
My, how good to see you.

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:21.730
Hello.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:22.600
Hello.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:26.820
I've been thinking about
renovating my building,

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.700
and was hoping you could
give me an estimate on the work.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.410
It would be my pleasure.

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:35.120
I'm going to take a quick look. Would you
mind waiting here a moment, Letty?

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.450
Of course not!

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.870
I heard you're looking
for parents for a chick!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.620
Everyone's talking about it.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:43.540
Is that true?

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.630
Oh, uh...

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:48.050
If you don't want it, then give it to me!

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:59.730
Dwarves'll pay a high price
for rare creatures!

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:03.150
I'd make a nice chunk of pocket change!

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:07.070
This guy seems super sketchy!

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:09.570
This is bad!

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:13.860
We're <i>not </i>selling it to the dwarves!
Not in a million years!

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.740
Why not? Not like you
know what to do with it.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.540
No way, no how!

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:21.870
Fine, then, how about
one of those bear cubs?

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.580
Absolutely not!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.880
If you lay a single paw
on these kids, I'll...

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.210
You'll what?

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.340
I'll breathe fire on you!

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:44.100
I'll do it, you know. It's gonna be hot.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:49.980
Sorry, I didn't hear ya.
Head's too damn heavy.

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:53.240
C'mon, I'll treat 'em kindly.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:58.700
Don't make this harder
than it's gotta be, mmkay?

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:04.790
I knew I couldn't do this!

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:08.420
I'm not strong enough to protect anyone...

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:12.840
No, that doesn't matter.

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:17.850
I'm gonna protect them!

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:23.350
Hot! Hot! Burning! Hot!

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.430
DOT: Burns

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:26.270
Burning!

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:29.020
He may look harmless...

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:33.990
But some call him the
Flame Dragon Lord of Mass Destruction.

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.280
He's turned countless Heroes to ash

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:40.160
and razed a kingdom
to the ground in a single night.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.370
<i>He's </i>the Flame Dragon Lord?!

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:46.080
Run now, or risk being
turned into BBQ beef.

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:52.960
The Heroes have made you
quite famous, haven't they?

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.970
I don't wanna be famoush!

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:59.470
Thank you so much!

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.140
I was so scared, Dad!

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:05.310
But the dragon was so cool!

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:10.190
It suwe isn't easy being
a fathew. Good fow him.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:11.980
I've something to tell you, Letty.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:12.820
Huh?

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:14.570
Down, boy.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:31.790
You risked your life to protect them.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.590
You're a wonderful father.

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.220
Papa! Papa!

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:49.270
Thanks!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:02.990
I suppose we'll be looking for family-friendly
properties from here on out.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:05.540
Yes, if you wouldn't mind!

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:09.870
Have you decided on a name for it yet?

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:13.540
I had to think long
and hard on it, but yeah!

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.750
I named him Pip!

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.130
Not very long, then.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:23.140
His full name's Piyovelt Phelpia
Pi Alpine Piyoderika!

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:24.760
How cool is that?!

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.850
A doting father already, I see.

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:01.150
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:01.190
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:01.230
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:03.150
When looking for apartments in Japan,

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:05.780
one often hears the English words
"apartment" and "mansion."

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:08.950
But what exactly is the difference
between the two terms?

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:08.860
What's the difference between
'apartment' and 'mansion'?

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:11.750
Each brings to mind
a certain type of building,

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:10.070
2 floors

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:10.070
3+ floors

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:10.070
wooden

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:10.070
neighborly

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:10.070
security

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:10.070
Huge building

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
Apartment

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
Mansion

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
2 floors

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
3+ floors

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
wooden

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
neighborly

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
security

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.830
Huge building

00:23:11.750 --> 00:23:15.040
but the truth is,
neither have a set definition.

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:20.380
The property owners decide which
term to use to describe their units.

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:18.830
Looks like an 'apartment' to me!

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:20.830
And this here's a 'mansion'!

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:25.550
You also see the words "heights,"
"co-op," and "maison" in their names,

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:26.090
Heights

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:26.090
Co-Op

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:26.090
Maison

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:30.640
but those are also hand-picked by
owners and mean nothing in particular.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:30.720
Chimera

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:30.720
Empusa

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:30.720
Orthros

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:32.270
"Chateau" "Residence"

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:36.470
Chateau

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:36.470
Residence

00:23:32.270 --> 00:23:36.270
and "Palace,"

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:36.470
Palace

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:39.730
while you may associate those words
with castles and luxurious mansions,

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.770
Chateau

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.770
Residence

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.770
Palace

00:23:39.730 --> 00:23:43.610
note that many buildings may not be
as luxurious as their names would imply.

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:46.650
Palace Muscle Panther

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:46.570
Next time, "A Dragon In Trouble."

